Ferrivide sent every finding of the last round back to the engineer to fix in this change (R24):
#1 [must fix] README.md:45: The fingerprint check comes after the setup block (lines 36-43), and that block already runs `sudo apt update` and `sudo apt install`. The text says to check "before running `apt update`", but anyone who pastes the block in order has already trusted the key fetched from gh-pages and installed a package that runs as root. A substituted key would be caught too late, if at all. The check is a trust gate, so it has to come before the key is trusted. (Cyber reviewer (Opus 5.5))
   Suggested fix: Split the setup block into three steps: (1) the `curl … | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/cosmic-ext-nightlight.gpg` line; (2) `gpg --show-keys --with-fingerprint …`, the expected fingerprint, and a line saying "if it differs, delete the file and stop"; (3) the `echo deb … | sudo tee`, `sudo apt update` and `sudo apt install` lines. Optionally, check the key before it reaches /usr/share/keyrings: download it to a temporary file, check its fingerprint, then dearmor it into place.
#2 [should fix] README.md:45: The task asked to replace a placeholder with the fingerprint, but the base README has no placeholder and release.yml has no grep for one. The agent added a new instruction block instead, and nothing in the change or its report says the premise didn't match. Either confirm with the user where the placeholder was supposed to be, or say in the report that the section is new, and that the fingerprint check is a new user-facing step. (Quick reviewer (Haiku 5.5))
   Suggested fix: Report to the user that no placeholder existed on this branch. Keep the new section only if the user wants it, and confirm the fingerprint against the signing key before merge. Do not add the placeholder token anywhere.
#3 [suggestion] README.md:45: The text says to compare the fingerprint "before running `apt update`", but the preceding code block already runs `apt update` and `apt install`. Readers will have installed before they verify. (Sonnet 5.5)
   Suggested fix: Split the setup block: download and dearmor the key, then show the fingerprint check, then add the sources list and run `apt update` and `apt install`. Or reword to "compare it, and remove the key if it differs".

